@description Rea-Sixty
@author Frank Acklin
@version 0.2
@changelog
  - Codename: There's always money in the banana-stand.
  - New: Channel-Strip Switch — 8 favourite Channel Strips swap in place, carrying values across by engineering value + meaning (favourites must be mapped)
  - New: Touch-to-Learn — touch a control and wiggle a parameter to bind it on the fly, without opening Settings
  - New: Rotary Step cycle — put a plug-in's button/enum options on a V-Pot or UC1 knob (turn to scrub, press to step)
  - New: Parameter Groups mirror an unmapped, identical plug-in 1:1 across group members — no mapping needed
  - New: Focus Set — pin the focused track (or a chosen set) to the left of the surface
  - New: Solo/Mute modifier modes — hold a keyboard modifier + Solo/Cut for REAPER's solo/mute button modes (UF8 + UC1)
  - New: V-Pot pan now records track-pan automation in Touch and holds
  - New: empty UF8 channels park the fader fully down
  - New: user-definable SSL CS/BC free soft-key slots + coherent factory banks
  - New: in-app manual is searchable and rewritten in plain, user-facing language
  - Fix: JSFX continuous knobs resolve finely; binary on/off knob flips per detent; Learn-HUD nil-crash; CS-Switch value-transfer robustness; Windows build
